.git/
docs/
tests/
scripts/*
!scripts/generate-runtime-sbom.py
!scripts/cargo_lock.py
# tools/toolbox/Dockerfile builds from this same context and reads its pinned
# tool versions out of the tree rather than restating them. These enter the
# context only; the appliance image never copies them, so its contents and its
# runtime-sha256.manifest are unchanged.
!scripts/install-hadolint.sh
!scripts/install-trivy.sh
!tests/requirements-dev.txt
*.md
*.log
*.tar.gz
output/
build/
.build/
work/
env/
.github/
.githooks/
# Leading **/ is required: an unanchored "__pycache__/" only matches the build
# context root, so nested bytecode such as src/omt_client/__pycache__ would be
# copied into the image and hashed into runtime-sha256.manifest, making the
# image depend on whatever the build machine happened to compile locally.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
vars.yml
